# **The rule that makes awk awk.** A field that looks like a number compares as
# one, so `$1 < $2` on `10 9` is false -- while `"10" < "9"` is true, because
# two string literals are two strings. POSIX calls the first a *strnum*, and it
# is the single semantic this language has that nothing else here does.
args: '{ print ($1 < $2), ("10" < "9"), ($1 == 10) }'
input:
10 9
2 10
0 x
